Body:
(I use Opus 4.6) Am I missing out something? Is it fixed or not? I still see premium requests burn-out. But yesterday I used opencode for a long horizon task & it worked great using just 2-3 premium requests (I really want it to work like that always), otherwise normally it uses half of my monthly premium requests. How can we fix it? Also I have below config, is it really a fix? 

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "agent": {
    "title": {
      "model": "github-copilot/gpt-4.1"
    },
    "summary": {
      "model": "github-copilot/gpt-5-mini"
    }
  },
  "mcp": {
    "playwright": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": [
        "npx",
        "@playwright/mcp@latest"
      ],
      "enabled": true
    }
  }
}
```

I didn't change model for the compaction & all other things, because it was degrading my output. I really need the fix soon, I can't survive this way whole month.

This is working for me in opencode.
```json
"provider": {
    "kimicoding": {
      "models": {
        "kimi-for-coding": {
          "name": "kimi-for-coding"
        }
      },
      "name": "Kimi",
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/anthropic",
      "options": {
        "apiKey": "<your-kimi-api-key>",
        "baseURL": "https://api.kimi.com/coding/v1"
      }
    }
  }
```
